    <section class="rise-fall" id="timeline" aria-labelledby="timeline-title">
      <h2 class="profile-section-title" id="timeline-title">Timeline</h2>
      <ol class="rf-events"><li><span class="rf-year">c. 1500–1200 BCE</span><span class="rf-text">The hymns of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rigveda">Rigveda</a>, the oldest Hindu scripture, are composed in north-west <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">c. 700–500 BCE</span><span class="rf-text">The earliest <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upanishads">Upanishads</a> explore the identity of the self (atman) and ultimate reality (Brahman)</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">c. 400 BCE–400 CE</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahabharata">Mahabharata</a>, with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhagavad-gita">Bhagavad Gita</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramayana">Ramayana</a> take shape</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">c. 320–550</span><span class="rf-text">Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gupta-empire">Gupta Empire</a>, temple building, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puranas">Puranas</a> and devotion to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vishnu">Vishnu</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shiva">Shiva</a> flourish</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">8th century</span><span class="rf-text">Shankara teaches Advaita <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vedanta">Vedanta</a>, the non-dual reading of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upanishads">Upanishads</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">early 12th century</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angkor-wat">Angkor Wat</a> is built as a temple to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vishnu">Vishnu</a> under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-empire">Khmer</a> king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suryavarman-ii">Suryavarman II</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1893</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swami-vivekananda">Swami Vivekananda</a> introduces Hinduism to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/worlds-parliament-of-religions">World’s Parliament of Religions</a> in Chicago</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1950</span><span class="rf-text">The constitution of the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> abolishes untouchability</span></li></ol>
    </section>

